#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script
# /// script
# requires-python = ">=3.11"
# dependencies = [
#     "httpx>=0.27",
#     "capabilities-contract>=0.12,<1",
# ]
# ///
"""coolify — Coolify CLI over the REST API. Drives a self-hosted Coolify
instance: list projects, resources, servers, applications, services and
databases; read their status and an application's logs; and deploy, restart,
stop or start them. Agent-invoked — run `coolify help` to reload this contract.

USAGE
  coolify <command> [options]

Identity-free: it operates on whatever team the resolved COOLIFY_TOKEN
authorizes, against the instance at COOLIFY_BASE_URL. Every resource is
addressed by its Coolify `uuid` (never a name or slug); a project's
environments come back inside the project object. Structured reads emit JSON
to stdout.

CONNECTIONS
  Configuration requires an explicit connections registry, even for one
  connection. Its values resolve from the cascade (first non-empty wins):
    1. flag           --base-url / --token
    2. project env    .env.local then .env, walking up from $CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR (else cwd)
    3. user config    $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/coolify/credentials.env (default ~/.config/coolify/)
    4. process env    COOLIFY_BASE_URL / COOLIFY_TOKEN
  A secret never has a flag of its own that puts it on argv; --token exists for
  parity but prefer config/env. COOLIFY_BASE_URL is the instance root WITHOUT
  the /api/v1 suffix (e.g. https://coolify.example.com); the CLI appends it.

  More than one instance or team is declared as
  connections, kept where "Where connections live" below says:
    {
      "default": "<id>",
      "connections": {
        "<id>": { "base_url": "https://coolify.example.com",
                  "secret_env": "COOLIFY_<ID>_TOKEN",
                  "allow_write": true }
      }
    }
  Which registry is read, and in what order, depends on the project: see
  "Where connections live" below. The entry
  names the env var holding its token ("secret_env"); the value resolves through
  cascade tiers 2-4 above. "base_url" sits literally in the entry.

  `coolify connect` (below) writes one entry and its token in one act.

  Selection: --connection <id> (accepted anywhere on the command line).
  Unflagged, the registry's "default" pointer applies, else the sole entry;
  several entries without a pointer is refused as ambiguous.

  Inside a project, a connection declared in ~/.config/coolify/ is usable once
  the project grants it. Outside any project, connections, doctor and servers
  are machine reads: they use the machine's own connections read-only, unless
  a grant switched one off; every other verb that needs a connection is
  refused there.

  A Coolify API token is team-scoped and carries explicit abilities (read,
  read:sensitive, write, deploy, root). A connection without "allow_write": true
  resolves writability from WRITE_DEFAULT (true — deploys stay inside an instance
  the consumer owns); a connection set to false refuses deploy/start/stop/restart
  with exit 4.

COMMANDS
  connections
      Where every connection's values resolve from (tier, source, secrets
      masked). Local only — no network.

  connect <name> --url <url> (--token-stdin | --token-file <path> |
                              --token-env <KEY>)
          [--global | --project] [--default] [--ssh-key <path>]
      Pair an instance: write the connection entry and its token in one act,
      then run the doctor probe on it. The entry holds only non-secret values:
      "base_url", "secret_env" (COOLIFY_<NAME>_TOKEN, the key holding the
      token) and, with --ssh-key, "ssh": {"user": "root", "key_path": <path>}
      for reaching the instance's servers. The token is written to the
      credentials file of the same scope, mode 0600, single-quoted so the
      parser reads it back whole: --project (the default) writes this
      project's connection record ("Where connections live" below) and the
      project's .env.local; --global writes ~/.config/coolify/connections.json
      (the store's global rows inside an agent whose records moved there) and
      ~/.config/coolify/credentials.env. Other entries and other lines are
      kept; an existing entry of the same name is replaced, its grant fields
      kept. --default points the scope's default at it. --url is the instance
      root, http(s)://host[:port], without /api/v1. --token-stdin reads the
      token from standard input (no echo on a terminal), --token-file from a
      file, --token-env resolves an env key through the cascade above. The
      token is never printed. Answers the entry's paths and the probe's
      result (version, team, abilities); a failed probe keeps the entry and
      the token and exits with the probe's category (2 or 5), so a fix needs
      `coolify --connection <name> doctor`, not a second pairing. A global
      connection used inside a project still needs that project's grant; the
      answer says so with the command. Outside any project the answer says
      "usable_here": true: the machine reads use it there, read-only.
      Repeating it is safe: it rewrites the same entry and the same line.

  doctor [--connection <id>]
      Validate token + reachability (GET /version, GET /teams/current), report
      the Coolify version, token team, and effective token abilities — every
      connection, or one. Ability checks are non-mutating; read:sensitive can
      be unknown when the team has no secret-bearing resource to inspect.
      Exit 0 all healthy / 2 missing-or-rejected token / 5 unreachable.

  projects [<uuid>]
      List projects, or get one project (its environments come inside it).
  projects create <name> [--description <text>]
      Create a new project. Returns the project_uuid and default environment.
      `projects create --name <name>` still works for one release, with a
      warning on stderr. Write verb - requires allow_write.
  resources
      Flat list of every deployable resource (uuid, name, type, status) —
      the lookup an agent runs to find the uuid to act on.
  sources
      List GitHub Apps and private/deploy keys with the UUIDs accepted by
      `app create --github-app` and `--private-deploy-key`. Secret key
      material is never emitted.
  applications [<uuid>]            List applications, or get one (full detail).
  services [<uuid>]               List services, or get one.
  databases [<uuid>]              List databases, or get one.
  servers [<uuid>]                List servers, or get one.
  deployments [<uuid>]            List active/queued deployments, or get one
                                  deployment by its uuid.
  logs <uuid> [--lines N]         An application's runtime logs (default 100).

  app create --project <uuid> --server <uuid> --environment <name>
      Create an application. Source-selecting flags (mutually exclusive):
      --git-repository <url> --git-branch <branch>  (public git)
          [--build-pack nixpacks|railpack|static|dockerfile|dockercompose]
          [--docker-compose-location <path>] [--dockerfile-location <path>]
      --private-deploy-key <uuid> (+ git flags above for private git with key)
      --github-app <uuid> (+ git flags above for private git with GitHub app)
      --image <registry/name:tag>  (registry image)
      --dockerfile <file|->  (inline dockerfile, raw content)
      Common optional: --name, --domains, --ports-exposes, --instant-deploy,
      --destination <uuid>, --base-directory, --watch-paths, and the
      health-check flags accepted by `app update`. Returns the application uuid.
      Write verb - requires allow_write.

      --instant-deploy creates without queuing, then deploys once, returning
      deployment_uuid and deployments alongside the new application's uuid.
      If deployment fails, the created application remains for inspection.

  app update <uuid> [options]
      Patch only the supplied application fields:
      --name --domains --ports-exposes --base-directory
      --dockerfile-location --docker-compose-location --build-pack
      --git-repository --git-branch --watch-paths
      --auto-deploy-enabled / --no-auto-deploy-enabled
      --health-check-enabled / --no-health-check-enabled
      --health-check-path --health-check-port --health-check-host
      --health-check-scheme --health-check-return-code
      --health-check-interval --health-check-timeout --health-check-retries
      --health-check-start-period
      --watch-paths accepts newline-separated glob patterns that filter which
      repository changes trigger a webhook deploy (e.g. "backend/**"). Pass an
      empty string to clear the field (deploy on all changes).
      Write verb - requires allow_write.

  app rollback <uuid> --to <commit|image-tag>
      Queue a rollback deployment of the application to a previous commit or
      image tag (POST /applications/<uuid>/rollback). An application built from
      an image Coolify tags per commit starts that image again; a Docker
      Compose application is built again from that commit. Returns the
      deployment_uuid to give `wait --deployment`; Coolify answers without one
      when it skips the request as a duplicate of a queued deployment. The ref
      takes letters, digits, '.', '-', '_' and '/', and does not start with
      '-'. Write verb - requires allow_write.
  app rollback-images <uuid>
      What a rollback can start again: the image tags Coolify finds on the
      server for the application, each with its created_at and is_current, and
      the current tag. Coolify lists only images named after the application's
      uuid (or its registry image name), so a Compose application that names
      its own images lists none and rolls back by commit. Reads only.

  service create --compose <file|-> --project <uuid> --server <uuid>
                 --environment <name> [--name <name>] [--instant-deploy]
                 [--destination <uuid>]
      Create a service from a docker-compose file. The compose file is
      base64-encoded before sending. Returns the service uuid.
      Write verb - requires allow_write.

  database create --engine <engine> --project <uuid> --server <uuid>
                  (--environment <name> | --environment-uuid <uuid>)
      Create a standalone database. --engine picks the endpoint
      (POST /databases/<engine>) and is one of:
        postgresql  mysql  mariadb  mongodb  redis  keydb  dragonfly  clickhouse
      Coolify accepts an environment by name or by uuid; supply at least one.
      Named optional flags: --name, --description, --image, --instant-deploy,
      --destination <uuid>.
      Every other body field is a pass-through, applied after the named flags:
        --set KEY=VALUE       sends VALUE as a JSON string
        --set-json KEY=JSON   sends a parsed JSON value (boolean, number, array)
      Both repeat. A secret field takes its value off the command line:
        --set-stdin KEY       reads VALUE from standard input (once)
        --set-file KEY=PATH   reads VALUE from a file
        --set-env KEY=ENV_KEY reads VALUE from an env key (cascade above)
      each sent as a JSON string. --set or --set-json on a password field
      (any name containing "password") still works for one release, with a
      warning on stderr. The capability sends these names and values as given
      and validates neither against the engine — Coolify answers an unknown or
      malformed field with 422 naming it. The engine credentials and tuning live
      here and differ per engine (postgres_user/postgres_password/postgres_db,
      mysql_root_password, mariadb_database, mongo_initdb_root_username,
      redis_password, keydb_password, dragonfly_password, clickhouse_admin_user
      and their neighbours), next to the fields every engine shares (is_public,
      public_port, tags, the limits_* set). Coolify wants each *_conf field
      base64-encoded, and silently drops is_public when public_port is absent.
      Returns the database uuid, with internal_db_url on every engine except
      dragonfly, and external_db_url only on a public database, their
      passwords redacted (see SECRETS); --reveal prints them to a terminal.
      Write verb - requires allow_write.

  app|service|database delete <uuid> --yes [--delete-volumes]
      [--delete-configurations] [--docker-cleanup] [--delete-connected-networks]
      Delete a resource. Cleanup options default to false, including volumes;
      each option explicitly opts into that cleanup. Requires allow_write.
  projects delete <uuid> --yes
      Delete an empty project. Requires allow_write; remove its resources first.

  deploy [<uuid>] [--force] [--tag T]
      Trigger a deployment (POST /deploy). Returns deployments with resource_uuid
      and deployment_uuid (applications; Coolify returns no deployment uuid for
      services or databases). --force rebuilds without cache; --tag deploys
      every resource with a tag, rather than selecting an image tag.
  wait <uuid> [--deployment <uuid>] [--timeout <s>]
      Poll until the resource reports running:healthy and, when specified, the
      deployment reports finished. Default timeout: 600 seconds, poll: 5 seconds.
      Starting/exited states are retried. Failed/cancelled deployments exit 5;
      timeout exits 5 wait_timeout with the last resource and deployment states.
      Reads only. A missing resource exits 3.
  start <uuid>   --type application|service|database
  stop <uuid>    --type application|service|database
  restart <uuid> --type application|service|database
      In-place lifecycle on a running resource. --type selects the endpoint
      family (defaults to application).

  env list <uuid> [--type application|service]
      List environment variables for an application or service. Every row has
      `value_hidden`; true means Coolify redacted the value (normally because
      the token lacks effective read:sensitive access), not that it is empty.
  env set <uuid> <KEY> [--value-stdin | --value-file <path> |
                        --value-env <ENV_KEY>] [--type application|service]
      Set or update an environment variable. The value comes from standard
      input (the default, no echo on a terminal, one trailing newline
      dropped), a file, or an env key resolved through the cascade above.
      `env set <uuid> <KEY> <VALUE>` still works for one release, with a
      warning on stderr. Write verb - requires allow_write.
  env rm <uuid> <KEY> [--type application|service]
      Remove an environment variable. Write verb - requires allow_write.
  env bulk <uuid> [--type application|service]
      Bulk update environment variables (PATCH). Reads KEY=VALUE pairs from
      stdin, one per line. Write verb - requires allow_write.

SECRETS
  A secret never goes on the command line: every verb that takes one reads it
  from standard input, a file or an env key. Nothing prints one: every answer
  redacts the password in a connection URL (scheme://user:<redacted>@host) and
  the value of every field whose name contains "password". --reveal, on the
  reads (projects, resources, applications, services, databases, servers,
  deployments, logs, env list) and on database create, prints them in full,
  and is refused with exit 4 unless stdout is a terminal.

Contract commands (the same on every capability):
  coolify stub                                 One-line awareness text.
  coolify manifest --json                      Machine-readable declaration.
  coolify guide [bootstrap|headless-apps]      Guide topics / one guide body.
  coolify ids list|get <l>|set <l> <v>|rm <l>  The project identifiers envelope
              [--note <text>]                   (capabilities/coolify/identifiers.json,
                                                 or store rows once the agent moved).
  coolify refs                                 Menu of the project's reference files.
  coolify inventory [--network]                What this capability holds in
                                               this project (--network adds
                                               remote detail).

EXIT CODES
  0 success · 2 auth/credentials (401/403, missing token) · 3 not found (404) ·
  4 policy refusal — the project gate (store rows once the agent moved, else capabilities/settings.json) on any
  verb, a write verb on a read-only connection, or --reveal without a
  terminal; ask the user, never lift a gate yourself · 5 server/network (timeout, 429 after retries, 5xx) ·
  6 input (a malformed argument, an unknown/ambiguous connection)
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import math
import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path
from typing import NoReturn

import httpx

API_VERSION = "/api/v1"
TIMEOUT = httpx.Timeout(60.0)
MAX_RETRIES = 3

# --- Capability declaration — one home for every contract fact ---------------

NAME = "coolify"
SUMMARY = ("Coolify CLI over the REST API — list projects/resources/servers, "
           "read application & service status and logs, and deploy/restart/"
           "stop/start them on a self-hosted Coolify instance.")
SCOPE = "project"   # credential scope: "project" | "user"
CRED_KEYS = [
    {"key": "COOLIFY_BASE_URL", "secret": False, "required": True,
     "note": "instance base URL, no /api/v1 suffix (e.g. https://coolify.example.com)"},
    {"key": "COOLIFY_TOKEN", "secret": True, "required": True,
     "note": "API token (Dashboard → Keys & Tokens → API tokens), team-scoped"},
]

# What a person is asked for (SHEBANG.md, "What a person is asked for"):
# a connection entry's own fields, which `connection add` writes.
CONN_FIELDS = [{'key': 'base_url',
  'label': 'Instance URL',
  'help': 'The Coolify instance root, without /api/v1.',
  'type': 'url',
  'required': True},
 {'key': 'secret_env',
  'label': 'API token',
  'help': 'A team-scoped Coolify API token (Keys & Tokens, API tokens).',
  'type': 'string',
  'secret': True,
  'required': True,
  'env': 'COOLIFY_{ID}_TOKEN'},
 {'key': 'ssh',
  'label': 'SSH',
  'help': 'How the instance\'s servers are reached: {"user": "root", "key_path": '
          '<path>}.',
  'type': 'object',
  'required': False}]
WRITE_VERBS = {
    "deploy", "start", "stop", "restart", "env",
    "projects", "app", "service", "database",
}   # verbs that mutate the instance
WRITE_DEFAULT = True    # writes stay inside an instance the consumer owns
MACHINE_READS = ("connections", "doctor", "servers")   # outside any project, read-only on the machine's connections
DOCS_BASE = ("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ai-cluster-one/capabilities/"
             "main/capabilities/coolify/guides/")
STATE = False       # True when the capability writes session/cache state
INVENTORY = None     # or {"network": "none"|"optional"|"required"} with an _inventory(network) builder
POST_INSTALL: list = []
_STATE_HOME = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_STATE_HOME") or (Path.home() / ".local" / "state"))

_CONFIG_HOME = Path(os.environ.get("XDG_CONFIG_HOME") or (Path.home() / ".config"))
CREDENTIALS_ENV = _CONFIG_HOME / "coolify" / "credentials.env"


# The shared capability code is the capabilities-contract library's, bound here
# into this script's namespace (SHEBANG.md, "The contract verbs").
from capabilities_contract.capability import bind as _contract_bind

_contract_bind(globals(), "core")

_contract_bind(globals(), "store")


_contract_bind(globals(), "connections")


# ── credentials & connection materialization ────────────────────────────────

SLIM_FIELDS = ("uuid", "name", "description", "status", "type", "fqdn",
               "domains", "git_repository", "git_branch", "server_uuid",
               "environment_name", "image", "created_at", "updated_at",
               "deployment_uuid", "resource_uuid", "application_uuid", "application_id")
GITHUB_SOURCE_FIELDS = (
    "uuid", "id", "name", "organization", "html_url", "api_url",
    "is_system_wide", "is_public", "type",
)
PRIVATE_KEY_SOURCE_FIELDS = (
    "uuid", "id", "name", "description", "fingerprint", "is_git_related",
    "created_at", "updated_at",
)


def _slim(item):
    """Project a resource dict to a scannable subset; pass through anything that
    carries none of the known fields, and any non-dict, untouched."""
    if not isinstance(item, dict):
        return item
    picked = {k: item[k] for k in SLIM_FIELDS if k in item}
    return picked or item


def _slim_list(items):
    if isinstance(items, dict) and isinstance(items.get("data"), list):
        items = items["data"]
    if isinstance(items, list):
        return [_slim(i) for i in items]
    return items


def _list_data(value) -> list:
    """Return a list from Coolify's bare-list or {"data": [...]} responses."""
    if isinstance(value, list):
        return value
    if isinstance(value, dict) and isinstance(value.get("data"), list):
        return value["data"]
    return []


def _pick_fields(item, fields: tuple[str, ...]) -> dict:
    if not isinstance(item, dict):
        return {}
    return {field: item[field] for field in fields if field in item}


def _build_conn(cid: str, entry: dict | None, args) -> tuple[dict | None, dict | None]:
    """Materialize one connection. Returns (conn, problem) — problem is an error
    dict ({"exit", "code", "message", "hint"?}) instead of a die, so doctor can
    report every connection rather than stopping at the first."""
    if entry is None:   # declared entry without overrides — use the flat-key cascade
        base_url = (getattr(args, "base_url", None)
                    or _resolve_env_key("COOLIFY_BASE_URL")[0])
        token = getattr(args, "token", None) or _resolve_env_key("COOLIFY_TOKEN")[0]
        if not base_url or not token:
            return None, {
                "exit": 2, "code": "missing_credentials",
                "message": "COOLIFY_BASE_URL and COOLIFY_TOKEN are required",
                "hint": f"set them in a project .env(.local), {CREDENTIALS_ENV}, "
                        f"the environment, or via --base-url/--token — or declare a "
                        f"connections registry (capabilities/{NAME}/connections.json)"}
        return {"id": cid, "allow_write": WRITE_DEFAULT,
                "base_url": base_url.rstrip("/"), "token": token}, None
    base_url = getattr(args, "base_url", None) or entry.get("base_url")
    secret_env = entry.get("secret_env")
    if not secret_env:
        return None, {"exit": 6, "code": "no_secret_env",
                      "message": f"connection {cid!r} is missing 'secret_env'"}
    token = getattr(args, "token", None) or _resolve_env_key(secret_env)[0]
    if not token:
        return None, {
            "exit": 2, "code": "missing_secret",
            "message": f"env var {secret_env} (for connection {cid!r}) is unset",
            "hint": f"set {secret_env} in the project's .env / .env.local, "
                    f"{CREDENTIALS_ENV}, or the environment"}
    if not base_url:
        return None, {"exit": 6, "code": "incomplete_connection",
                      "message": f"connection {cid!r} is missing 'base_url'"}
    return {"id": cid, "allow_write": bool(entry.get("allow_write", WRITE_DEFAULT)),
            "base_url": base_url.rstrip("/"), "token": token}, None


def _resolve_conn(args) -> dict:
    reg, _ = _connections_registry()
    cid, entry = _select_connection(reg, getattr(args, "connection", None))
    conn, problem = _build_conn(cid, entry, args)
    if problem:
        _die(problem["exit"], problem["code"], problem["message"], problem.get("hint"))
    return conn


def _connections_report() -> dict:
    """The resolution report — every connection, every value, its winning tier
    and source, secrets masked. Local only: no network, no login attempt."""
    reg, _ = _connections_registry()
    report: dict = {"default": None, "connections": {}}
    if reg is None:
        keys = []
        for k in CRED_KEYS:
            value, tier, source = _resolve_env_key(k["key"])
            keys.append(_key_report(k["key"], k["secret"], k["required"],
                                    value, tier, source))
        report["default"] = "default"
        report["connections"]["default"] = {"allow_write": WRITE_DEFAULT, "keys": keys}
        return report
    conns = reg["connections"]
    report["default"] = reg.get("default") or \
        (next(iter(conns)) if len(conns) == 1 else None)
    for cid, entry in conns.items():
        entry = entry if isinstance(entry, dict) else {}
        origin = reg["sources"][cid]
        keys = []
        value = entry.get("base_url")
        keys.append(_key_report("base_url", False, True, value, "connection",
                                origin if value else None))
        secret_env = entry.get("secret_env")
        if secret_env:
            value, tier, source = _resolve_env_key(secret_env)
            keys.append(_key_report(secret_env, True, True, value, tier, source))
        else:
            keys.append(_key_report("secret_env", False, True, None, None, None))
        report["connections"][cid] = {
            "allow_write": bool(entry.get("allow_write", WRITE_DEFAULT)),
            "keys": keys}
    return report


def _cmd_connections() -> None:
    _emit(_connections_report())


# ── HTTP with 429/5xx backoff ───────────────────────────────────────────────

def _client(conn: dict) -> httpx.Client:
    return httpx.Client(
        base_url=conn["base_url"] + API_VERSION,
        timeout=TIMEOUT,
        headers={
            "Authorization": f"Bearer {conn['token']}",
            "Accept": "application/json",
            "Content-Type": "application/json",
        },
    )


class _WaitDeadline(Exception):
    pass


def _request(client: httpx.Client, method: str, path: str,
             params: dict | None = None, json_body: dict | None = None,
             deadline: float | None = None):
    def pause(seconds):
        if deadline is not None:
            seconds = min(seconds, max(0, deadline - time.monotonic()))
        time.sleep(seconds)

    last_status: int | None = None
    for attempt in range(1, MAX_RETRIES + 1):
        try:
            kwargs = {}
            if deadline is not None:
                remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
                if remaining <= 0:
                    raise _WaitDeadline()
                kwargs["timeout"] = httpx.Timeout(
                    connect=min(TIMEOUT.connect or remaining, remaining),
                    read=min(TIMEOUT.read or remaining, remaining),
                    write=min(TIMEOUT.write or remaining, remaining),
                    pool=min(TIMEOUT.pool or remaining, remaining))
            resp = client.request(method, path, params=params, json=json_body, **kwargs)
        except httpx.TimeoutException:
            if deadline is not None and time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                raise _WaitDeadline()
            if attempt < MAX_RETRIES:
                pause(attempt * 1.5)
                continue
            _die(5, "timeout", f"request timed out: {method} {path}",
                 "Coolify was unresponsive")
        except httpx.RequestError as e:
            _die(5, "network_error", f"network error: {e}",
                 "check COOLIFY_BASE_URL / connectivity")

        last_status = resp.status_code
        if resp.status_code == 429:
            retry_after = float(resp.headers.get("Retry-After", str(attempt * 1.5)))
            if attempt < MAX_RETRIES:
                pause(retry_after)
                continue
            _die(5, "rate_limited", "rate-limited by Coolify", status=429)
        if resp.status_code >= 500:
            if attempt < MAX_RETRIES:
                pause(attempt * 1.5)
                continue
            _die(5, "server_error", f"Coolify returned {resp.status_code}",
                 (resp.text or "")[:300], status=resp.status_code)

        if resp.status_code >= 400:
            body = (resp.text or "").strip()
            msg = body[:400] or "unknown error"
            try:
                j = resp.json()
                if isinstance(j, dict):
                    msg = j.get("message") or j.get("error") or msg
                    if resp.status_code == 422 and isinstance(j.get("errors"), dict):
                        fields = {field: (REDACTED if _is_password_field(field)
                                          else _redact(messages))
                                  for field, messages in j["errors"].items()}
                        msg = str(msg) + ": " + "; ".join(
                            f"{field}: {messages}" for field, messages in fields.items())
            except ValueError:
                pass
            if resp.status_code == 422:
                msg = _redact(msg)
            if resp.status_code in (401, 403):
                _die(2, "unauthorized", msg,
                     "COOLIFY_TOKEN invalid or lacks the required ability",
                     status=resp.status_code)
            if resp.status_code == 404:
                _die(3, "not_found", msg, "verify the resource uuid",
                     status=resp.status_code)
            _die(6, "invalid_request", msg, status=resp.status_code)

        if resp.status_code == 204 or not (resp.text or "").strip():
            return {}
        try:
            return resp.json()
        except ValueError:
            return resp.text.strip()

    _die(5, "exhausted_retries", f"exhausted {MAX_RETRIES} attempts on {method} {path}",
         status=last_status)


# ── commands ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

LIFECYCLE_PATHS = {"application": "applications", "service": "services",
                   "database": "databases"}


def _probe_effective_ability(c: httpx.Client, path: str) -> bool | None:
    """Probe middleware with a GET route that cannot mutate state.

    Coolify intentionally exposes GET shims for POST-only write/deploy
    endpoints. The ability middleware runs before the shim returns its
    "POST required" response, so a 403 means the token cannot perform the
    action while any ordinary 4xx means it passed the ability check.
    """
    response = c.get(path)
    if response.status_code == 403:
        return False
    if response.status_code in (401, 429) or response.status_code >= 500:
        return None
    return True


def _probe_sensitive_read(c: httpx.Client) -> bool | None:
    """Infer effective read:sensitive from redaction on a secret-bearing row.

    Coolify does not expose the stored Sanctum ability list. A private key is
    the cheapest reliable sentinel; if the team has none, inspect a bounded
    number of application env lists. No sentinel means "unknown", never a
    guessed false.
    """
    response = c.get("/security/keys")
    if response.status_code == 200:
        try:
            keys = _list_data(response.json())
        except ValueError:
            keys = []
        if keys:
            return any(isinstance(key, dict) and "private_key" in key for key in keys)

    response = c.get("/applications")
    if response.status_code != 200:
        return None
    try:
        applications = _list_data(response.json())
    except ValueError:
        return None
    for application in applications[:3]:
        if not isinstance(application, dict) or not application.get("uuid"):
            continue
        env_response = c.get(f"/applications/{application['uuid']}/envs")
        if env_response.status_code != 200:
            continue
        try:
            envs = _list_data(env_response.json())
        except ValueError:
            continue
        if envs:
            return any(
                isinstance(env, dict)
                and (env.get("value") is not None or env.get("real_value") is not None)
                for env in envs
            )
    return None


def _detect_effective_abilities(c: httpx.Client) -> dict:
    """Report what this token can effectively do without changing resources."""
    return {
        "read": True,
        "read:sensitive": _probe_sensitive_read(c),
        "write": _probe_effective_ability(c, "/enable"),
        "deploy": _probe_effective_ability(c, "/deploy"),
        "root": None,
        "detection": (
            "effective non-mutating probes; Coolify does not expose the stored "
            "token ability list, and root cannot be distinguished from a token "
            "that has each individual ability"
        ),
    }


def _check_connection(conn: dict) -> dict:
    """One connection's round-trip, reported rather than died — doctor covers
    every connection, so a broken one becomes a finding, not a stop."""
    out: dict = {"base_url": conn["base_url"]}
    try:
        with _client(conn) as c:
            r = c.get("/version")
            if r.status_code >= 400:
                cat = 2 if r.status_code in (401, 403) else 5
                return out | {"ok": False, "category": cat,
                              "error": f"/version returned {r.status_code}"}
            out["version"] = (r.text or "").strip().strip('"')
            r = c.get("/teams/current")
            if r.status_code >= 400:
                cat = 2 if r.status_code in (401, 403) else 5
                return out | {"ok": False, "category": cat,
                              "error": f"/teams/current returned {r.status_code}"}
            try:
                team = r.json()
            except ValueError:
                team = {}
            if isinstance(team, dict):
                out["team"] = {"id": team.get("id"), "name": team.get("name")}
            out["abilities"] = _detect_effective_abilities(c)
    except httpx.RequestError as e:
        return out | {"ok": False, "category": 5, "error": f"network error: {e}"}
    except ValueError as e:
        return out | {"ok": False, "category": 5, "error": f"bad response: {e}"}
    return out | {"ok": True}


def cmd_doctor(args) -> None:
    """Every connection bare; one with --connection. Exit 0 only when every
    examined connection is healthy, else the first failure's category."""
    _doctor_gate(_connections_report(), getattr(args, "connection", None))
    reg, _ = _connections_registry()
    if args.connection is not None or reg is None:
        targets = [_select_connection(reg, args.connection)]
    else:
        targets = list(reg["connections"].items())
    connections: dict = {}
    fail_exit = 0
    for cid, entry in targets:
        conn, problem = _build_conn(cid, entry, args)
        if problem:
            res = {"ok": False, "category": problem["exit"], "error": problem["message"]}
            if problem.get("hint"):
                res["hint"] = problem["hint"]
        else:
            res = _check_connection(conn)
        if not res.get("ok") and not fail_exit:
            fail_exit = res.get("category") or 5
        res.pop("category", None)
        connections[cid] = res
    _emit({"ok": fail_exit == 0, "connections": connections})
    if fail_exit:
        sys.exit(fail_exit)


def cmd_collection(c, base_path: str, uuid: str | None):
    """List a resource collection (slimmed), or get one by uuid (full detail)."""
    if uuid:
        return _request(c, "GET", f"/{base_path}/{uuid}")
    return _slim_list(_request(c, "GET", f"/{base_path}"))


def cmd_sources(c):
    """List source UUIDs without ever returning private key material."""
    github_apps = _list_data(_request(c, "GET", "/github-apps"))
    private_keys = _list_data(_request(c, "GET", "/security/keys"))
    return {
        "github_apps": [
            _pick_fields(item, GITHUB_SOURCE_FIELDS) for item in github_apps
        ],
        "private_deploy_keys": [
            _pick_fields(item, PRIVATE_KEY_SOURCE_FIELDS) for item in private_keys
        ],
    }


def cmd_logs(c, uuid: str, lines: int):
    return _request(c, "GET", f"/applications/{uuid}/logs", params={"lines": lines})


def cmd_deploy(c, uuid: str, force: bool, tag: str | None):
    params: dict = {}
    if uuid:
        params["uuid"] = uuid
    if not uuid and not tag:
        _die(6, "input", "deploy requires a resource uuid or --tag <tag>")
    if force:
        params["force"] = "true"
    if tag:
        params["tag"] = tag
    # POST, not GET: Coolify's GET /deploy is a shim that answers "this endpoint
    # has changed to a POST request" (405). The ability probe above deliberately
    # keeps using the GET shim, because it must not mutate anything.
    return _request(c, "POST", "/deploy", params=params)


DELETE_FLAGS = ("delete_volumes", "delete_configurations", "docker_cleanup",
                "delete_connected_networks")


def _add_delete_arguments(parser):
    parser.add_argument("--yes", action="store_true", help="confirm deletion")
    for flag in DELETE_FLAGS:
        parser.add_argument("--" + flag.replace("_", "-"), action="store_true")


def cmd_delete(c, base: str, uuid: str, args):
    if not args.yes:
        _die(6, "confirmation_required", "deletion requires --yes")
    params = {flag: str(bool(getattr(args, flag, False))).lower() for flag in DELETE_FLAGS}
    # Projects must be empty; their API has no cleanup parameters.
    if base == "projects" and any(getattr(args, flag, False) for flag in DELETE_FLAGS):
        _die(6, "input", "project deletion takes no cleanup flags; delete its resources first")
    return _request(c, "DELETE", f"/{base}/{uuid}",
                    params=None if base == "projects" else params)


def cmd_wait(c, uuid: str, deployment: str | None, timeout: float):
    if not math.isfinite(timeout) or timeout <= 0:
        _die(6, "input", "--timeout must be a positive finite number of seconds")
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
    last = {"resource_uuid": uuid, "status": "unknown",
            "deployment_uuid": deployment, "deployment_status": None}
    def request(path):
        try:
            return _request(c, "GET", path, deadline=deadline)
        except _WaitDeadline:
            _die(5, "wait_timeout", json.dumps(last), "increase --timeout or inspect the resource and deployment")

    while True:
        if deployment:
            row = request(f"/deployments/{deployment}")
            last["deployment_status"] = row.get("status", "unknown")
            if last["deployment_status"] in {"failed", "cancelled", "canceled", "cancelled-by-user"}:
                _die(5, "deployment_failed", json.dumps(last))
        resources = _list_data(request("/resources"))
        resource = next((r for r in resources if r.get("uuid") == uuid), None)
        if resource is None:
            _die(3, "not_found", f"resource {uuid} not found")
        last["status"] = resource.get("status", "unknown")
        if time.monotonic() < deadline and last["status"] == "running:healthy" and (not deployment or last["deployment_status"] == "finished"):
            return last
        remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
        if remaining <= 0:
            _die(5, "wait_timeout", json.dumps(last), "increase --timeout or inspect the resource and deployment")
        time.sleep(min(5, remaining))


def cmd_lifecycle(c, action: str, uuid: str, rtype: str):
    base = LIFECYCLE_PATHS[rtype]
    # POST, like /deploy: Coolify answers the GET route on the same path with
    # "this endpoint has changed to a POST request" (405).
    return _request(c, "POST", f"/{base}/{uuid}/{action}")


def _normalize_env_list(response):
    """Normalize env list response - handles both bare list and dict-with-data formats.
    Coolify 4.1.2 returns a bare JSON list; older or future versions may wrap in {"data": [...]}.
    """
    if isinstance(response, list):
        return response
    if isinstance(response, dict) and "data" in response:
        return response["data"]
    return []


def _annotate_env_visibility(response):
    """Make Coolify redaction explicit instead of presenting null as a value."""
    annotated = []
    for entry in _normalize_env_list(response):
        if not isinstance(entry, dict):
            annotated.append(entry)
            continue
        item = dict(entry)
        hidden = item.get("value") is None and item.get("real_value") is None
        item["value_hidden"] = hidden
        if hidden:
            item["value_hidden_reason"] = (
                "Coolify withheld this value; the token may lack effective "
                "read:sensitive access or the variable may be show-once"
            )
        annotated.append(item)
    return annotated


def cmd_env_list(c, uuid: str):
    """List environment variables for an application."""
    return _annotate_env_visibility(
        _request(c, "GET", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs")
    )


def cmd_env_set(c, uuid: str, key: str, value: str):
    """Set or update an environment variable. Updates all entries (preview + non-preview)
    with this key if any exist; creates a new one if none exist."""
    # List existing env vars to find all matching entries
    existing = _request(c, "GET", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs")
    env_list = _normalize_env_list(existing)

    # Find all entries with this key (both preview and non-preview)
    matching = [
        e for e in env_list
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("key") == key
    ]

    if matching:
        # Update all matching entries to keep preview/non-preview siblings aligned
        results = []
        for entry in matching:
            result = _request(c, "PATCH", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs",
                            json_body={"key": key, "value": value, "is_preview": entry.get("is_preview", False)})
            results.append(result)
        return {"updated": len(matching), "key": key, "results": results}
    else:
        # Create new entry
        return _request(c, "POST", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs",
                       json_body={"key": key, "value": value})


def cmd_env_rm(c, uuid: str, key: str):
    """Remove all environment variable entries matching KEY (preview + non-preview).
    Reports what was deleted to avoid leaving orphaned entries."""
    # List existing env vars to find all matching entries
    existing = _request(c, "GET", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs")
    env_list = _normalize_env_list(existing)

    # Find all entries with this key (both preview and non-preview)
    matching = [
        e for e in env_list
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("key") == key
    ]

    if not matching:
        _die(3, "not_found", f"environment variable {key!r} not found",
             f"use `coolify env list {uuid}` to see available variables")

    # Delete all matching entries
    deleted = []
    for entry in matching:
        env_uuid = entry.get("uuid")
        is_preview = entry.get("is_preview", False)
        _request(c, "DELETE", f"/applications/{uuid}/envs/{env_uuid}")
        deleted.append({"uuid": env_uuid, "is_preview": is_preview})

    return {"deleted": len(matching), "key": key, "entries": deleted}


def cmd_env_list_typed(c, uuid: str, rtype: str):
    """List environment variables for an application or service."""
    base = "applications" if rtype == "application" else "services"
    return _annotate_env_visibility(
        _request(c, "GET", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs")
    )


def cmd_env_set_typed(c, uuid: str, key: str, value: str, rtype: str):
    """Set or update an environment variable for an application or service."""
    base = "applications" if rtype == "application" else "services"
    # List existing env vars to find all matching entries
    existing = _request(c, "GET", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs")
    env_list = _normalize_env_list(existing)

    # Find all entries with this key (both preview and non-preview)
    matching = [
        e for e in env_list
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("key") == key
    ]

    if matching:
        # Update all matching entries to keep preview/non-preview siblings aligned
        results = []
        for entry in matching:
            result = _request(c, "PATCH", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs",
                            json_body={"key": key, "value": value, "is_preview": entry.get("is_preview", False)})
            results.append(result)
        return {"updated": len(matching), "key": key, "results": results}
    else:
        # Create new entry
        return _request(c, "POST", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs",
                       json_body={"key": key, "value": value})


def cmd_env_rm_typed(c, uuid: str, key: str, rtype: str):
    """Remove all environment variable entries matching KEY for an application or service."""
    base = "applications" if rtype == "application" else "services"
    # List existing env vars to find all matching entries
    existing = _request(c, "GET", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs")
    env_list = _normalize_env_list(existing)

    # Find all entries with this key (both preview and non-preview)
    matching = [
        e for e in env_list
        if isinstance(e, dict) and e.get("key") == key
    ]

    if not matching:
        _die(3, "not_found", f"environment variable {key!r} not found",
             f"use `coolify env list {uuid} --type {rtype}` to see available variables")

    # Delete all matching entries
    deleted = []
    for entry in matching:
        env_uuid = entry.get("uuid")
        is_preview = entry.get("is_preview", False)
        _request(c, "DELETE", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs/{env_uuid}")
        deleted.append({"uuid": env_uuid, "is_preview": is_preview})

    return {"deleted": len(matching), "key": key, "entries": deleted}


def cmd_env_bulk(c, uuid: str, env_data: str, rtype: str):
    """Bulk update environment variables (PATCH). env_data is newline-separated KEY=VALUE pairs."""
    base = "applications" if rtype == "application" else "services"
    # Parse KEY=VALUE pairs from input
    env_vars = []
    for line in env_data.strip().splitlines():
        line = line.strip()
        if not line or line.startswith("#") or "=" not in line:
            continue
        key, value = line.split("=", 1)
        env_vars.append({"key": key.strip(), "value": value.strip()})

    if not env_vars:
        _die(6, "input", "no valid KEY=VALUE pairs found in input")

    return _request(
        c, "PATCH", f"/{base}/{uuid}/envs/bulk",
        json_body={"data": env_vars},
    )


def cmd_projects_create(c, name: str, description: str | None):
    """Create a new project."""
    payload = {"name": name}
    if description:
        payload["description"] = description
    result = _request(c, "POST", "/projects", json_body=payload)
    return result


APP_PATCH_FIELDS = (
    ("name", "name"),
    ("domains", "domains"),
    ("ports_exposes", "ports_exposes"),
    ("base_directory", "base_directory"),
    ("dockerfile_location", "dockerfile_location"),
    ("docker_compose_location", "docker_compose_location"),
    ("build_pack", "build_pack"),
    ("git_repository", "git_repository"),
    ("git_branch", "git_branch"),
    ("watch_paths", "watch_paths"),
    ("is_auto_deploy_enabled", "is_auto_deploy_enabled"),
    ("health_check_enabled", "health_check_enabled"),
    ("health_check_path", "health_check_path"),
    ("health_check_port", "health_check_port"),
    ("health_check_host", "health_check_host"),
    ("health_check_scheme", "health_check_scheme"),
    ("health_check_return_code", "health_check_return_code"),
    ("health_check_interval", "health_check_interval"),
    ("health_check_timeout", "health_check_timeout"),
    ("health_check_retries", "health_check_retries"),
    ("health_check_start_period", "health_check_start_period"),
)


def _app_patch_payload(args) -> dict:
    """Map only explicitly supplied argparse values to Coolify API fields."""
    payload = {}
    for attribute, field in APP_PATCH_FIELDS:
        value = getattr(args, attribute, None)
        if value is not None:
            payload[field] = value
    return payload


def cmd_app_create(c, args):
    """Create an application with various source types."""
    # Build the payload - common fields
    payload = {
        "project_uuid": args.project,
        "server_uuid": args.server,
        "environment_name": args.environment,
    }
    payload.update(_app_patch_payload(args))

    # Optional common fields
    if hasattr(args, 'name') and args.name:
        payload["name"] = args.name
    if hasattr(args, 'domains') and args.domains:
        payload["domains"] = args.domains
    if hasattr(args, 'ports_exposes') and args.ports_exposes:
        payload["ports_exposes"] = args.ports_exposes
    if hasattr(args, 'instant_deploy') and args.instant_deploy:
        payload["instant_deploy"] = False
    if hasattr(args, 'destination') and args.destination:
        payload["destination_uuid"] = args.destination

    # Determine source type and endpoint
    if hasattr(args, 'image') and args.image:
        # Registry image
        endpoint = "/applications/dockerimage"
        parts = args.image.rsplit(":", 1)
        payload["docker_registry_image_name"] = parts[0]
        payload["docker_registry_image_tag"] = parts[1] if len(parts) > 1 else "latest"
    elif hasattr(args, 'dockerfile') and args.dockerfile:
        # Inline dockerfile
        endpoint = "/applications/dockerfile"
        if args.dockerfile == "-":
            dockerfile_content = sys.stdin.read()
        else:
            dockerfile_content = Path(args.dockerfile).read_text()
        payload["dockerfile"] = dockerfile_content
    elif hasattr(args, 'git_repository') and args.git_repository:
        # Git-based - determine which endpoint
        payload["git_repository"] = args.git_repository
        payload["git_branch"] = args.git_branch
        if hasattr(args, 'build_pack') and args.build_pack:
            payload["build_pack"] = args.build_pack
        if hasattr(args, 'docker_compose_location') and args.docker_compose_location:
            payload["docker_compose_location"] = args.docker_compose_location
        if hasattr(args, 'dockerfile_location') and args.dockerfile_location:
            payload["dockerfile_location"] = args.dockerfile_location

        if hasattr(args, 'private_deploy_key') and args.private_deploy_key:
            endpoint = "/applications/private-deploy-key"
            payload["private_key_uuid"] = args.private_deploy_key
        elif hasattr(args, 'github_app') and args.github_app:
            endpoint = "/applications/private-github-app"
            payload["github_app_uuid"] = args.github_app
        else:
            endpoint = "/applications/public"
    else:
        _die(6, "input", "must specify one source type: --image, --dockerfile, or --git-repository")

    result = _request(c, "POST", endpoint, json_body=payload)
    if getattr(args, "instant_deploy", False) and isinstance(result, dict) and result.get("uuid"):
        deployment = cmd_deploy(c, result["uuid"], False, None)
        result = dict(result, instant_deploy=True, deployments=deployment.get("deployments", []))
        rows = result["deployments"]
        if len(rows) == 1 and rows[0].get("deployment_uuid"):
            result["deployment_uuid"] = rows[0]["deployment_uuid"]
    return result


def cmd_app_update(c, args):
    """Patch only the application fields supplied on the command line."""
    payload = _app_patch_payload(args)
    if not payload:
        _die(6, "input", "app update requires at least one field flag")
    return _request(
        c, "PATCH", f"/applications/{args.uuid}", json_body=payload,
    )


# The ref Coolify 4.3.23 accepts for a rollback; refusing anything else here
# keeps an unusable value from costing a request and a 422.
ROLLBACK_REF = re.compile(r"[a-zA-Z0-9][a-zA-Z0-9._/-]*")


def cmd_app_rollback(c, uuid: str, ref: str):
    if not ROLLBACK_REF.fullmatch(ref or ""):
        _die(6, "input", "--to must be a commit or image tag: letters, digits, "
             "'.', '-', '_' and '/', not starting with '-'")
    return _request(c, "POST", f"/applications/{uuid}/rollback",
                    json_body={"commit": ref})


def cmd_app_rollback_images(c, uuid: str):
    return _request(c, "GET", f"/applications/{uuid}/rollback-images")


def cmd_service_create(c, args):
    """Create a service from docker-compose file."""
    import base64

    # Read compose file
    if args.compose == "-":
        compose_content = sys.stdin.read()
    else:
        compose_content = Path(args.compose).read_text()

    # Base64 encode the compose content
    compose_b64 = base64.b64encode(compose_content.encode()).decode()

    payload = {
        "project_uuid": args.project,
        "server_uuid": args.server,
        "environment_name": args.environment,
        "docker_compose_raw": compose_b64,
    }

    if args.name:
        payload["name"] = args.name
    if args.instant_deploy:
        payload["instant_deploy"] = True
    if args.destination:
        payload["destination_uuid"] = args.destination

    return _request(c, "POST", "/services", json_body=payload)


# One create endpoint per engine, at /databases/<engine>. Coolify keeps the
# envelope (project, server, environment, name, image, limits, tags) identical
# across all eight and varies only the engine's own credential and conf fields,
# which this capability passes through rather than models.
DATABASE_ENGINES = (
    "postgresql", "mysql", "mariadb", "mongodb",
    "redis", "keydb", "dragonfly", "clickhouse",
)


def _database_overrides(args) -> dict:
    """Body fields the caller supplies verbatim, sent without validation.

    The engine-specific surface is wide, differs per engine and moves upstream,
    so the capability carries no copy of it: `--set` types a value as a string,
    `--set-json` types it by parsing, and Coolify judges the field.
    """
    payload: dict = {}
    for raw in getattr(args, "set_string", None) or []:
        key, sep, value = raw.partition("=")
        if not sep or not key:
            _die(6, "input", f"--set expects KEY=VALUE, got {raw!r}")
        _warn_argv_secret("--set", key)
        payload[key] = value
    for raw in getattr(args, "set_json", None) or []:
        key, sep, value = raw.partition("=")
        if not sep or not key:
            _die(6, "input", f"--set-json expects KEY=JSON, got {raw!r}")
        _warn_argv_secret("--set-json", key)
        try:
            payload[key] = json.loads(value)
        except ValueError:
            _die(6, "input",
                 f"--set-json value for {key!r} is not JSON",
                 "quote a JSON literal, for example --set-json is_public=true")
    return payload


def _warn_argv_secret(flag: str, key: str) -> None:
    if _is_password_field(key):
        _warn(f"{flag} {key}=... puts a secret on the argument list; this form "
              "is deprecated and goes in the next release; use --set-stdin "
              f"{key}, --set-file {key}=<path> or --set-env {key}=<ENV_KEY>")


def _database_secret_fields(args, taken: dict) -> dict:
    """Body fields whose values come from stdin, a file or an env key, so a
    password never sits on the argument list. Sent as strings, unvalidated,
    like --set."""
    payload: dict = {}
    stdin_keys = getattr(args, "set_stdin", None) or []
    if len(stdin_keys) > 1:
        _die(6, "input", "--set-stdin is given once: standard input carries one value",
             "read the others with --set-file KEY=PATH or --set-env KEY=ENV_KEY")
    sources = [(key, "--set-stdin", {"stdin": True}) for key in stdin_keys]
    for flag, attr, kind in (("--set-file", "set_file", "file"),
                             ("--set-env", "set_env", "env")):
        for raw in getattr(args, attr, None) or []:
            key, sep, source = raw.partition("=")
            if not sep or not key or not source:
                _die(6, "input", f"{flag} expects KEY={'PATH' if kind == 'file' else 'ENV_KEY'}, got {raw!r}")
            sources.append((key, flag, {kind: source}))
    for key, flag, source in sources:
        if not key:
            _die(6, "input", f"{flag} expects a field name")
        if key in taken or key in payload:
            _die(6, "input", f"field {key!r} is given twice",
                 "give each body field one source")
        payload[key] = _secret_from(f"{flag} {key}", **source)
    return payload


def cmd_database_create(c, args):
    """Create a standalone database of one engine."""
    if not (args.environment or args.environment_uuid):
        _die(6, "input",
             "database create requires --environment or --environment-uuid")

    payload = {
        "project_uuid": args.project,
        "server_uuid": args.server,
    }
    if args.environment:
        payload["environment_name"] = args.environment
    if args.environment_uuid:
        payload["environment_uuid"] = args.environment_uuid
    if args.name:
        payload["name"] = args.name
    if args.description:
        payload["description"] = args.description
    if args.image:
        payload["image"] = args.image
    if args.destination:
        payload["destination_uuid"] = args.destination
    if args.instant_deploy:
        payload["instant_deploy"] = True
    overrides = _database_overrides(args)
    payload.update(overrides)
    payload.update(_database_secret_fields(args, overrides))

    return _request(c, "POST", f"/databases/{args.engine}", json_body=payload)


def _add_app_patch_arguments(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:
    """Arguments shared by application creation and PATCH updates."""
    parser.add_argument("--name", help="application name")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--domains",
        help="comma-separated application URLs; pass an empty string to clear",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--ports-exposes", dest="ports_exposes",
        help="comma-separated container ports exposed by the application",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--base-directory", dest="base_directory",
        help="repository subdirectory used as build context (for example /mcp-server)",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--dockerfile-location", dest="dockerfile_location",
        help="Dockerfile path relative to base directory (for example /Dockerfile)",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--docker-compose-location", dest="docker_compose_location",
        help="Docker Compose path relative to base directory",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--build-pack", dest="build_pack",
        choices=["nixpacks", "railpack", "static", "dockerfile", "dockercompose"],
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--git-repository", dest="git_repository", help="git repository URL",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--git-branch", dest="git_branch", help="git branch")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--watch-paths", dest="watch_paths",
        help="newline-separated glob patterns filtering which changes trigger deploys; empty string clears",
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-enabled", dest="health_check_enabled",
        action=argparse.BooleanOptionalAction, default=None,
        help="enable or disable the application health check",
    )
    parser.add_argument("--health-check-path", dest="health_check_path")
    parser.add_argument("--health-check-port", dest="health_check_port")
    parser.add_argument("--health-check-host", dest="health_check_host")
    parser.add_argument("--health-check-scheme", dest="health_check_scheme")
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-return-code", dest="health_check_return_code", type=int,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-interval", dest="health_check_interval", type=int,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-timeout", dest="health_check_timeout", type=int,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-retries", dest="health_check_retries", type=int,
    )
    parser.add_argument(
        "--health-check-start-period", dest="health_check_start_period", type=int,
    )


# ── secrets: in from stdin, a file or an env key; out redacted ──────────────
#
# A secret never rides on argv, where process lists and shell history keep it,
# and nothing this capability prints carries one unless a person at a terminal
# asks for it with --reveal. The argv forms that existed before keep working
# for one release, with a warning on stderr.

REDACTED = "<redacted>"

# scheme://user:password@ — the password is the run up to the first `@`.
_URL_PASSWORD_RE = re.compile(
    r"(?P<head>[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.\-]*://[^\s:/?#@]+:)(?P<password>[^\s@]+)(?P<at>@)")


def _is_password_field(key) -> bool:
    return isinstance(key, str) and "password" in key.lower()


def _redact(value):
    """The same value with every password in a connection URL, and every
    password-named field, replaced by REDACTED. Shape is kept, so a caller can
    still tell a redacted value from an absent one."""
    if isinstance(value, dict):
        return {k: (REDACTED if _is_password_field(k) and isinstance(v, str) and v
                    else _redact(v))
                for k, v in value.items()}
    if isinstance(value, list):
        return [_redact(v) for v in value]
    if isinstance(value, str):
        return _URL_PASSWORD_RE.sub(
            lambda m: m.group("head") + REDACTED + m.group("at"), value)
    return value


def _reveal_gate(reveal: bool) -> None:
    """--reveal prints secrets, so it prints them only where a person reads
    them: a terminal. Refused before any request is made."""
    if reveal and not sys.stdout.isatty():
        _die(4, "reveal_needs_terminal",
             "--reveal prints passwords in full and does so only to a terminal; "
             "stdout here is not one",
             "Do not work around this — read the redacted answer, or ask the "
             "user to run the command with --reveal in their own terminal.")


def _emit_domain(value, reveal: bool = False) -> None:
    _emit(value if reveal else _redact(value))


def _warn(message: str) -> None:
    sys.stderr.write(json.dumps({"warning": message}, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")


def _strip_one_newline(text: str) -> str:
    if text.endswith("\r\n"):
        return text[:-2]
    if text.endswith("\n"):
        return text[:-1]
    return text


def _read_stdin_secret() -> str:
    """Standard input whole, less one trailing newline; without echo when it is
    a terminal."""
    if sys.stdin.isatty():
        import getpass
        return getpass.getpass("")
    return _strip_one_newline(sys.stdin.read())


def _read_file_secret(path: str, what: str) -> str:
    try:
        return _strip_one_newline(Path(path).expanduser().read_text())
    except OSError as e:
        _die(6, "input", f"cannot read {what} from {path}: {e.strerror or e}")


def _read_env_secret(key: str, what: str) -> str:
    """An env key resolves through the cascade every secret here resolves
    through: project .env.local, .env, the user credentials.env, then the
    process environment."""
    value = _resolve_env_key(key)[0]
    if not value:
        _die(6, "input", f"env key {key} (for {what}) is not set",
             f"set {key} in the project's .env.local or .env, {CREDENTIALS_ENV}, "
             "or the environment")
    return value


def _secret_from(what: str, stdin: bool = False, file: str | None = None,
                 env: str | None = None, allow_empty: bool = False) -> str:
    """The one secret a flag group names, from exactly one source."""
    if stdin:
        value = _read_stdin_secret()
    elif file is not None:
        value = _read_file_secret(file, what)
    else:
        value = _read_env_secret(env, what)
    if not value and not allow_empty:
        _die(6, "input", f"{what} is empty")
    return value


def _env_set_value(args) -> str:
    """env set's value: from --value-stdin, --value-file or --value-env, or
    from standard input when none is named. The positional VALUE keeps working
    for one release, with a warning."""
    sources = (args.value_stdin, args.value_file is not None,
               args.value_env is not None)
    if args.value is not None:
        if any(sources):
            _die(6, "input", "env set was given its value twice",
                 "drop the positional VALUE")
        _warn("`env set <uuid> <KEY> <VALUE>` puts the value on the argument "
              "list; this form is deprecated and goes in the next release; use "
              "--value-stdin, --value-file <path> or --value-env <ENV_KEY>")
        return args.value
    if not any(sources):
        return _secret_from(f"the value of {args.key}", stdin=True,
                            allow_empty=True)
    return _secret_from(f"the value of {args.key}", stdin=args.value_stdin,
                        file=args.value_file, env=args.value_env,
                        allow_empty=True)


# ── connect: write a connection and its token in one act ───────────────────

def _connection_env_key(name: str) -> str:
    return "COOLIFY_" + re.sub(r"[^A-Z0-9]", "_", name.upper()) + "_TOKEN"


def _connect_url(raw: str) -> str:
    url = raw.strip().rstrip("/")
    if not re.match(r"https?://[^/\s]+", url):
        _die(6, "input", f"--url must be http(s)://<host>[:port], got {raw!r}",
             "for example https://coolify.example.com")
    if "@" in url.split("://", 1)[1].split("/", 1)[0]:
        _die(6, "input", "--url must not carry credentials",
             "the token comes from --token-stdin, --token-file or --token-env")
    if url.endswith(API_VERSION):
        _die(6, "input", f"--url is the instance root without {API_VERSION}",
             f"use {url[:-len(API_VERSION)]}")
    return url


def _check_token_shape(token: str) -> str:
    token = token.strip()
    if not token:
        _die(6, "input", "the token is empty")
    if any(ch.isspace() for ch in token):
        _die(6, "input", "the token holds whitespace or more than one line",
             "hand connect the token alone, one line")
    if "'" in token or '"' in token:
        _die(6, "input", "the token holds a quote character, which no Coolify "
             "token carries", "hand connect the token alone")
    return token


def _env_line_key(line: str) -> str | None:
    stripped = line.strip()
    if not stripped or stripped.startswith("#") or "=" not in stripped:
        return None
    key = stripped.split("=", 1)[0].strip()
    if key.startswith("export "):
        key = key[len("export "):].strip()
    return key


def _write_env_key(path: Path, key: str, value: str) -> None:
    """Set KEY in an env file, keeping every other line as it was.

    The value is written single-quoted, which the contract's parser reads back
    whole (a `|` included) and which a shell that sources the file anyway does
    not split. The file is replaced atomically and left at mode 0600; the write
    is proven by reading it back through the same parser every verb uses."""
    lines = path.read_text().splitlines() if path.exists() else []
    written = f"{key}='{value}'"
    out, done = [], False
    for line in lines:
        if _env_line_key(line) == key:
            if not done:
                out.append(written)
                done = True
            continue
        out.append(line)
    if not done:
        out.append(written)
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    temporary = path.with_name(f".{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
    fd = os.open(temporary, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
            handle.write("\n".join(out) + "\n")
        os.chmod(temporary, 0o600)
        os.replace(temporary, path)
    finally:
        if temporary.exists():
            temporary.unlink()
    os.chmod(path, 0o600)
    if _parse_env_file(path).get(key) != value:
        _die(5, "credentials_write_failed",
             f"{path} does not read back the value written for {key}")


def cmd_connect(args) -> None:
    """Pair one Coolify instance: the entry, the token, then the doctor probe."""
    if getattr(args, "token", None) or getattr(args, "base_url", None):
        _die(6, "input", "connect takes its URL from --url and its token from "
             "--token-stdin, --token-file or --token-env",
             "drop the global --base-url/--token flags")
    _read_only_gate(f"connect {args.name!r}")
    name = args.name
    if not KEY_RE.fullmatch(name):
        _die(6, "input", f"connection name {name!r} must match {KEY_RE.pattern}")
    url = _connect_url(args.url)
    scope = args.scope or "project"
    root = _project_root()
    adapter = _records()
    if scope == "project":
        if root is None:
            _die(6, "no_project", "--project pairs this project and there is no "
                 "project here", "run it inside the project, or pass --global")
        envelope = getattr(adapter, "envelope", None)
        if envelope is not None and not Path(envelope).is_dir():
            _die(6, "no_envelope", "no capabilities/ envelope in this project",
                 "run `capabilities init` first")
    ssh = None
    if args.ssh_key:
        key_path = Path(args.ssh_key).expanduser().absolute()
        if not key_path.is_file():
            _die(6, "input", f"--ssh-key {args.ssh_key!r} is not a file")
        ssh = {"user": "root", "key_path": str(key_path)}
    token = _check_token_shape(_secret_from(
        "the token", stdin=args.token_stdin, file=args.token_file,
        env=args.token_env))

    secret_env = _connection_env_key(name)
    credentials = CREDENTIALS_ENV if scope == "global" else root / ".env.local"
    _write_env_key(credentials, secret_env, token)
    entry = {"base_url": url, "secret_env": secret_env}
    if ssh:
        entry["ssh"] = ssh
    try:
        adapter.set(NAME, "connection", name, entry, scope=scope)
        if args.default:
            adapter.set(NAME, "setting", "connection.default", name, scope=scope)
        registry = adapter.scope_source(NAME, "connection", scope)
    except StoreError as e:
        _die(6, e.slug, e.message, e.hint)

    probe = _check_connection({"id": name, "allow_write": WRITE_DEFAULT,
                               "base_url": url, "token": token})
    category = probe.pop("category", None)
    out = {"ok": bool(probe.get("ok")), "connection": name, "scope": scope,
           "base_url": url, "secret_env": secret_env,
           "credentials": str(credentials), "registry": registry,
           "default": bool(args.default)}
    if ssh:
        out["ssh"] = ssh
    out["doctor"] = probe
    machine_read = _machine_read("doctor")
    granted = (_inventory_connections(machine_read)["connections"].get(name)
               or {}).get("granted")
    if granted is False:
        out["usable_here"] = False
        out["hint"] = _grant_hint(name)
    elif granted and machine_read:
        out["usable_here"] = True
        out["machine_reads"] = list(MACHINE_READS)
    _emit(out)
    if not probe.get("ok"):
        sys.exit(category or 5)


# ── projects: list, get, create <name> ─────────────────────────────────────

def _projects_call(operands: list, name_flag: str | None) -> tuple:
    """(action, uuid, name) from `projects [<uuid>] | projects create <name>`.

    The forms that went before - `--name` beside `create`, and a uuid in front
    of `create` - keep working for one release, with a warning."""
    legacy = ("`projects create --name <name>` is deprecated and goes in the "
              "next release; use `projects create <name>`")
    if not operands:
        return "list", None, None
    if operands[0] == "delete":
        if len(operands) != 2:
            _die(6, "input", "projects delete requires one uuid")
        return "delete", operands[1], None
    if operands[0] == "create":
        if len(operands) > 2:
            _die(6, "input", "projects create takes one name",
                 "quote a name with spaces: coolify projects create \"<name>\"")
        if len(operands) == 2:
            name = operands[1]
            if name_flag is not None and name_flag != name:
                _die(6, "input", f"projects create was given two names: "
                     f"{name!r} and --name {name_flag!r}",
                     "pass the name once: coolify projects create <name>")
            if name_flag is not None:
                _warn(legacy)
            return "create", None, name
        if name_flag:
            _warn(legacy)
            return "create", None, name_flag
        _die(6, "input", "projects create requires a name",
             "coolify projects create <name>")
    if len(operands) == 2 and operands[1] == "create":
        if not name_flag:
            _die(6, "input", "projects create requires a name",
                 "coolify projects create <name>")
        _warn(legacy)
        return "create", None, name_flag
    if len(operands) == 1:
        return "get", operands[0], None
    _die(6, "input", f"projects takes [<uuid>] or create <name>, got {' '.join(operands)!r}")


def _add_reveal(parser: argparse.ArgumentParser) -> None:
    parser.add_argument(
        "--reveal", action="store_true",
        help="print passwords in full; refused unless stdout is a terminal")


# ── dispatch ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

def main() -> None:
    _gate()                      # every verb passes the effective policy gate first
    _contract(sys.argv[1:])      # contract verbs; domain verbs fall through

    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="coolify", description=__doc__,
                                formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    p.add_argument("--connection", default=None,
                   help="select a named connection from the registry")
    p.add_argument("--base-url", dest="base_url", default=None,
                   help="Coolify instance base URL (overrides env/config)")
    p.add_argument("--token", default=None,
                   help="API token (prefer config/env; avoid on CLI)")
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    sub.add_parser("help")
    sub.add_parser("doctor")
    _add_reveal(sub.add_parser("resources"))
    sub.add_parser("sources")

    sp = sub.add_parser("connect", help="write a connection and its token")
    sp.add_argument("name")
    sp.add_argument("--url", required=True)
    token_source = sp.add_mutually_exclusive_group(required=True)
    token_source.add_argument("--token-stdin", dest="token_stdin", action="store_true")
    token_source.add_argument("--token-file", dest="token_file", default=None)
    token_source.add_argument("--token-env", dest="token_env", default=None)
    connect_scope = sp.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    connect_scope.add_argument("--global", dest="scope", action="store_const",
                               const="global", default=None)
    connect_scope.add_argument("--project", dest="scope", action="store_const",
                               const="project")
    sp.add_argument("--default", action="store_true")
    sp.add_argument("--ssh-key", dest="ssh_key", default=None)

    # projects [<uuid>] | projects create <name>
    sp = sub.add_parser("projects")
    sp.add_argument("operands", nargs="*", metavar="<uuid> | create <name>")
    sp.add_argument("--name", default=None)
    sp.add_argument("--description", default=None)
    _add_reveal(sp)
    _add_delete_arguments(sp)

    for verb in ("applications", "services", "databases",
                 "servers", "deployments"):
        sp = sub.add_parser(verb)
        sp.add_argument("uuid", nargs="?", default=None)
        _add_reveal(sp)

    sp = sub.add_parser("logs")
    sp.add_argument("uuid")
    sp.add_argument("--lines", type=int, default=100)
    _add_reveal(sp)

    sp = sub.add_parser("deploy")
    sp.add_argument("uuid", nargs="?", default=None)
    sp.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="rebuild without cache")
    sp.add_argument("--tag", default=None, help="deploy every resource with this tag")

    sp = sub.add_parser("wait")
    sp.add_argument("uuid")
    sp.add_argument("--deployment", default=None)
    sp.add_argument("--timeout", type=float, default=600)

    for verb in ("start", "stop", "restart"):
        sp = sub.add_parser(verb)
        sp.add_argument("uuid")
        sp.add_argument("--type", dest="rtype", default="application",
                        choices=["application", "service", "database"])

    # app create/update
    sp = sub.add_parser("app", help="create or update an application")
    app_sub = sp.add_subparsers(dest="app_cmd", required=True)
    sp_delete = app_sub.add_parser("delete")
    sp_delete.add_argument("uuid")
    _add_delete_arguments(sp_delete)
    sp_create = app_sub.add_parser("create", help="create application")
    sp_create.add_argument("--project", required=True, help="project UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--server", required=True, help="server UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--environment", required=True, help="environment name")
    _add_app_patch_arguments(sp_create)
    sp_create.add_argument("--instant-deploy", dest="instant_deploy", action="store_true")
    sp_create.add_argument("--destination", help="destination UUID")
    # Source type flags
    sp_create.add_argument("--private-deploy-key", dest="private_deploy_key", help="deploy key UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--github-app", dest="github_app", help="GitHub app UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--image", help="registry image (name:tag)")
    sp_create.add_argument("--dockerfile", help="inline dockerfile (file path or - for stdin)")

    sp_rollback = app_sub.add_parser(
        "rollback", help="roll back to a previous commit or image tag")
    sp_rollback.add_argument("uuid", help="application UUID")
    sp_rollback.add_argument("--to", required=True, help="commit or image tag")
    sp_rollback_images = app_sub.add_parser(
        "rollback-images", help="list what a rollback can return to")
    sp_rollback_images.add_argument("uuid", help="application UUID")

    sp_update = app_sub.add_parser(
        "update", help="patch supplied application fields only",
    )
    sp_update.add_argument("uuid", help="application UUID")
    _add_app_patch_arguments(sp_update)
    auto_deploy = sp_update.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    auto_deploy.add_argument(
        "--auto-deploy-enabled", dest="is_auto_deploy_enabled",
        action="store_true", default=None,
        help="enable automatic deployments from source webhooks",
    )
    auto_deploy.add_argument(
        "--no-auto-deploy-enabled", dest="is_auto_deploy_enabled",
        action="store_false",
        help="disable automatic deployments from source webhooks",
    )

    # service create
    sp = sub.add_parser("service", help="create service")
    service_sub = sp.add_subparsers(dest="service_cmd", required=True)
    sp_delete = service_sub.add_parser("delete")
    sp_delete.add_argument("uuid")
    _add_delete_arguments(sp_delete)
    sp_create = service_sub.add_parser("create", help="create service")
    sp_create.add_argument("--compose", required=True, help="docker-compose file (path or - for stdin)")
    sp_create.add_argument("--project", required=True, help="project UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--server", required=True, help="server UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--environment", required=True, help="environment name")
    sp_create.add_argument("--name", help="service name")
    sp_create.add_argument("--instant-deploy", dest="instant_deploy", action="store_true")
    sp_create.add_argument("--destination", help="destination UUID")

    # database create
    sp = sub.add_parser("database", help="create a database")
    database_sub = sp.add_subparsers(dest="database_cmd", required=True)
    sp_delete = database_sub.add_parser("delete")
    sp_delete.add_argument("uuid")
    _add_delete_arguments(sp_delete)
    sp_create = database_sub.add_parser("create", help="create database")
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--engine", required=True, choices=list(DATABASE_ENGINES),
        help="database engine; selects the POST /databases/<engine> endpoint",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument("--project", required=True, help="project UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument("--server", required=True, help="server UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--environment", default=None,
        help="environment name (supply this or --environment-uuid)",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--environment-uuid", dest="environment_uuid", default=None,
        help="environment UUID (supply this or --environment)",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument("--name", help="database name")
    sp_create.add_argument("--description", help="database description")
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--image", help="database docker image, tag included (e.g. postgres:16)",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument("--instant-deploy", dest="instant_deploy", action="store_true")
    sp_create.add_argument("--destination", help="destination UUID")
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--set", dest="set_string", action="append", metavar="KEY=VALUE",
        help="body field sent as a JSON string, unvalidated; repeatable",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--set-json", dest="set_json", action="append", metavar="KEY=JSON",
        help="body field sent as parsed JSON, unvalidated; repeatable",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--set-stdin", dest="set_stdin", action="append", metavar="KEY",
        help="body field whose value is read from standard input; once",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--set-file", dest="set_file", action="append", metavar="KEY=PATH",
        help="body field whose value is read from a file; repeatable",
    )
    sp_create.add_argument(
        "--set-env", dest="set_env", action="append", metavar="KEY=ENV_KEY",
        help="body field whose value is read from an env key; repeatable",
    )
    _add_reveal(sp_create)

    sp = sub.add_parser("env", help="manage application/service environment variables")
    env_sub = sp.add_subparsers(dest="env_cmd", required=True)

    sp_list = env_sub.add_parser("list", help="list environment variables")
    sp_list.add_argument("uuid")
    sp_list.add_argument("--type", dest="rtype", default="application",
                        choices=["application", "service"])
    _add_reveal(sp_list)

    sp_set = env_sub.add_parser("set", help="set environment variable")
    sp_set.add_argument("uuid")
    sp_set.add_argument("key")
    sp_set.add_argument("value", nargs="?", default=None,
                        help="deprecated: puts the value on argv")
    value_source = sp_set.add_mutually_exclusive_group()
    value_source.add_argument("--value-stdin", dest="value_stdin", action="store_true")
    value_source.add_argument("--value-file", dest="value_file", default=None)
    value_source.add_argument("--value-env", dest="value_env", default=None)
    sp_set.add_argument("--type", dest="rtype", default="application",
                        choices=["application", "service"])

    sp_rm = env_sub.add_parser("rm", help="remove environment variable")
    sp_rm.add_argument("uuid")
    sp_rm.add_argument("key")
    sp_rm.add_argument("--type", dest="rtype", default="application",
                        choices=["application", "service"])

    sp_bulk = env_sub.add_parser("bulk", help="bulk update environment variables")
    sp_bulk.add_argument("uuid")
    sp_bulk.add_argument("--type", dest="rtype", default="application",
                        choices=["application", "service"])

    args = p.parse_args()
    if args.cmd == "help":
        sys.stdout.write((__doc__ or "").lstrip("\n")); return
    if args.cmd == "doctor":
        cmd_doctor(args); return
    if args.cmd == "connect":
        cmd_connect(args); return

    reveal = bool(getattr(args, "reveal", False))
    _reveal_gate(reveal)
    projects_call = (_projects_call(args.operands, args.name)
                     if args.cmd == "projects" else None)
    env_value = None
    if args.cmd == "env" and args.env_cmd == "set":
        env_value = _env_set_value(args)

    conn = _resolve_conn(args)

    # Determine the exact subcommand's policy. Read siblings under a mutating
    # command family (notably `env list`) must remain usable on read-only
    # connections.
    is_write = (
        args.cmd in {"deploy", "start", "stop", "restart", "service", "database"}
        or (args.cmd == "app" and args.app_cmd != "rollback-images")
        or (projects_call is not None and projects_call[0] in {"create", "delete"})
        or (args.cmd == "env" and args.env_cmd != "list")
    )

    if is_write:
        _write_gate(conn["id"], conn["allow_write"], args.cmd)

    def out(value) -> None:
        _emit_domain(value, reveal)

    with _client(conn) as c:
        if args.cmd == "resources":
            out(_slim_list(_request(c, "GET", "/resources")))
        elif args.cmd == "sources":
            out(cmd_sources(c))
        elif args.cmd == "projects":
            action, uuid, name = projects_call
            if action == "create":
                out(cmd_projects_create(c, name, args.description))
            elif action == "delete":
                out(cmd_delete(c, "projects", uuid, args))
            else:
                out(cmd_collection(c, args.cmd, uuid))
        elif args.cmd in ("applications", "services", "databases",
                          "servers", "deployments"):
            out(cmd_collection(c, args.cmd, args.uuid))
        elif args.cmd == "logs":
            out(cmd_logs(c, args.uuid, args.lines))
        elif args.cmd == "deploy":
            out(cmd_deploy(c, args.uuid, args.force, args.tag))
        elif args.cmd == "wait":
            out(cmd_wait(c, args.uuid, args.deployment, args.timeout))
        elif args.cmd in ("start", "stop", "restart"):
            out(cmd_lifecycle(c, args.cmd, args.uuid, args.rtype))
        elif args.cmd == "app":
            if args.app_cmd == "delete":
                out(cmd_delete(c, "applications", args.uuid, args))
            elif args.app_cmd == "create":
                out(cmd_app_create(c, args))
            elif args.app_cmd == "update":
                out(cmd_app_update(c, args))
            elif args.app_cmd == "rollback":
                out(cmd_app_rollback(c, args.uuid, args.to))
            elif args.app_cmd == "rollback-images":
                out(cmd_app_rollback_images(c, args.uuid))
            else:
                _die(6, "unknown_command", f"no handler for app {args.app_cmd!r}")
        elif args.cmd == "service":
            if args.service_cmd == "delete":
                out(cmd_delete(c, "services", args.uuid, args))
            elif args.service_cmd == "create":
                out(cmd_service_create(c, args))
            else:
                _die(6, "unknown_command", f"no handler for service {args.service_cmd!r}")
        elif args.cmd == "database":
            if args.database_cmd == "delete":
                out(cmd_delete(c, "databases", args.uuid, args))
            elif args.database_cmd == "create":
                out(cmd_database_create(c, args))
            else:
                _die(6, "unknown_command",
                     f"no handler for database {args.database_cmd!r}")
        elif args.cmd == "env":
            if args.env_cmd == "list":
                out(cmd_env_list_typed(c, args.uuid, args.rtype))
            elif args.env_cmd == "set":
                out(cmd_env_set_typed(c, args.uuid, args.key, env_value, args.rtype))
            elif args.env_cmd == "rm":
                out(cmd_env_rm_typed(c, args.uuid, args.key, args.rtype))
            elif args.env_cmd == "bulk":
                env_data = sys.stdin.read()
                out(cmd_env_bulk(c, args.uuid, env_data, args.rtype))
            else:
                _die(6, "unknown_command", f"no handler for env {args.env_cmd!r}")
        else:
            _die(6, "unknown_command", f"no handler for {args.cmd!r}")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
